{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Behold, the man was as one of Us.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the Holy One, blessed be He, says 'of Us' in reference to the angels. And it should have said 'as one of you,' but out of His humility He included Himself with them. And the intent of the verse is to say that thus at first, before the first man sinned, he was entirely intellectual, with no impediment at all; and now he descended from his level and was invested with desires, and wished to know good and evil." "<b>And now, lest he stretch out his hand.</b> That is: since he has sinned and I have decreed death upon him, I need to prevent him from the tree of life, so that My decree not be nullified." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'Behold, the man was' — the first man was twenty years old, and this is 'the man was.' From here that a heavenly court does not punish until twenty years of age. And upon this basis the decree was issued upon the generation of the wilderness: 'from twenty years old and upward.' And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: 'twenty — to pursue,' for they pursue him from heaven to punish him for his sin." "<b>And the sense</b> of 'as one of Us' — our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded it. Rabbi Yehudah and Rabbi Shimon say: 'like the unique one of the world,' as it is said (Deuteronomy 6): ״שמע ישראל״ and so forth. The Rabbis say: 'like Gavriel,' as it is said (Ezekiel 9): ״ואיש אחד בתוכם לבוש הבדים״. 'Like this kamtza, whose garment is of it.' Know that there is a difference between אחד with a segol and אחד with a patach: for אחד with a segol stands by itself, not uniting with another that would be like it; but אחד with a patach is one that unites with another that is not like it, and it is a word attached to its kind, as in (Daniel 10): ״אחד השרים הראשונים״ — which unites with the rest of the branches of Ḥesed. And likewise (Genesis 32): ״אחד עשר ילדיו״. (ibid. 37): ״ואחד עשר כוכבים״. And this difference was known among these sages. And what Rabbi Yehudah understood from this — 'like the unique one of the world' — it appears to me his intent was to say that in an unpointed Torah scroll one could read כאחד ממנו with a segol. But the Rabbis who said 'like Gavriel' said so because Scripture did not write כאחד with a segol, and therefore they understood 'as one' like that which unites with the rest of the branches of Judgment like itself, and that is Gavriel. And what is written of him, ״ואיש אחד בתוכם״, is said only by way of transference; and the explanation of 'like this kamtza' comes to allude to the power of mercy within him, for they likened him to linen, which is a white garment, and this is the expression ״לבוש הבדים״ — wrapped in the tallit of mercy; and to tell you that even though he is the prince of Gevurah, the power of mercy is within him to merit the meritorious, and the power of mercy is not separated from him like this garment, which is of his very self and never departs from him." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'Behold, the man was' — like 'the man was,' and 'Moshe was,' and from here a hint that we are not in the beginning, and for this reason the Torah mentioned the birth of children in the language of 'knowledge,' and know this. And the view of Rabbi Yehudah who says 'like the unique one of the world' may possibly allude to the middle line, which is included from this and from that, and this is the secret of the verse (Song 3): ״עמודיו עשה כסף רפידתו זהב מרכבו ארגמן״. That is to say, that it is blended with various kinds of hues of light. And from here the secret of the formation of man will be explained — composite of two inclinations and included from them: the good inclination and the evil inclination, and these are what the masters of truth, upon them be peace, said: two ministering angels accompany a man, one on his right and one on his left."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:09.247876413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}